---
/**
 * Privacy Policy — static page. Concise, real policy matching what the
 * app actually does: no accounts; Google Analytics for aggregate usage
 * stats; graphs and settings stay in the browser.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Graphing Calculator: no accounts, Google Analytics for aggregate usage stats, and your graphs stay in your browser."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  mainClass="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:py-14"
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Last updated: September 29, 2026</p>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
    <p>
      The Graphing Calculator is designed to work without collecting your personal data. This policy
      describes, in plain terms, what happens with your information.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts or sign-ups. To understand aggregate usage, the site uses Google
      Analytics, which collects usage data such as pages visited, device and browser type, and
      approximate location. Browsing the site, plotting functions, and saving graphs send no
      personal information — like your name or email — to any server, because the site never asks
      for it.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">AI assistant</h2>
    <p>
      When you send a message to the AI math assistant, your message and a compact summary of your
      current calculator state (expressions, viewport) are sent to the site&rsquo;s own server
      endpoint (<code>/api/ai/math</code>). If an AI provider key is configured, the server forwards
      your message to the AI provider (DeepSeek) to generate a response. The server never logs your
      messages or any API key; rate-limiting state is kept only in memory and expires within
      minutes.
    </p>
    <p>
      When no provider key is configured, the assistant runs in a clearly labeled
      <em>mock mode</em>: responses are generated by deterministic local logic and no AI provider is
      contacted. Local intents (for example, &ldquo;plot y = x^2&rdquo;) are handled entirely in
      your browser and never reach a server.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Google Analytics sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) to recognize returning visitors and
      measure aggregate usage. These are the only third-party cookies on the site; there is no
      advertising. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or use Google&rsquo;s
      Analytics opt-out browser add-on, without breaking the calculator.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
      What stays in your browser
    </h2>
    <p>
      Your theme preference and your calculator workspace (expressions, viewport, settings) are
      stored only in your own browser&rsquo;s localStorage. They never leave your device. Clearing
      your browser&rsquo;s site data removes them permanently.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this policy, email
      <a
        href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}
        class="font-medium text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400"
      >
        {siteConfig.contactEmail}
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">
      This policy will be updated if the product&rsquo;s data practices change. The last-updated
      date above always reflects the current version.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
